# Incremental implementation

Adapted from https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills (incremental-implementation).

Build in thin vertical slices. Each increment leaves the system working and testable.

**Increment cycle:** Implement the smallest complete piece → Test → Verify (tests pass / build
ok / manual check) → Commit → next slice. Carry forward, don't restart.

**Slicing:**
- **Vertical** (preferred): one complete path through the stack (DB + API + UI) per slice.
- **Contract-first**: define the API contract (types/OpenAPI), then build backend + frontend
  against it in parallel, then integrate. Fits the PRD 002 → 003 split.
- **Risk-first**: prove the riskiest piece first (e.g. NSE cookie/fetch, the WebSocket) before
  building on it.

**Rule 0 — simplicity first:** ask "what's the simplest thing that could work?" before coding.
Don't write more than ~100 lines before testing. Only skip this for single-file, single-function
changes.
